---
import PathwayLandingLayout from '../../layouts/PathwayLandingLayout.astro';
import { getPathwayCategoryHero } from '@/lib/pathwayHeroes';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '@/lib/seo/config';

const title = 'EB-5 Concurrent Filing for U.S. Visa Holders | StudentEB5';
const metaDescription =
  'EB-5 concurrent filing for U.S. visa holders explains filing I-526E with adjustment of status, including EAD and advance parole concepts, with links to official USCIS processing times.';
const canonicalUrl = `${SITE_CONFIG.url}/pathways/eb5-concurrent-filing`;
const h1 = 'EB-5 Concurrent Filing for U.S. Visa Holders';
const subhead =
  'What it means to file your EB-5 petition together with adjustment of status when you are already in the United States on valid nonimmigrant status.';

const relatedResearch = [
  {
    title: 'J-1, F-1, H-1B Concurrent Filing with EB-5: Full Guide',
    url: '/research/j1-f1-h1b-eb5-concurrent-filing',
    description: 'Technical depth on concurrent filing across common nonimmigrant statuses.',
  },
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Investment Process',
    url: '/eb5-investment-process',
    description: 'Step-by-step filing sequence from source of funds through I-829.',
  },
];
const hero = getPathwayCategoryHero('process-mechanics');

---

<PathwayLandingLayout
  title={title}
  metaDescription={metaDescription}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  h1={h1}
  subhead={subhead}
  heroImage={hero.image}
  heroImageWebp={hero.webp}
  heroImageAlt="EB-5 pathway for EB-5 concurrent filing"
  relatedResearch={relatedResearch}
  secondaryCtaText="Talk to Someone About Concurrent Filing"
  breadcrumbTitle="EB-5 Concurrent Filing"
  keywords={[
    'EB-5 concurrent filing',
    'I-526E I-485 concurrent',
    'EB-5 EAD advance parole',
    'EB-5 work authorization',
  ]}
>
  <h2>Concurrent filing vs. consular processing</h2>
  <p>
    If you are already in the U.S. on a valid nonimmigrant status and a visa number is available (or other eligibility
    rules allow it), concurrent filing generally means submitting Form I-526E together with an adjustment of status
    package, including applications that can lead to interim work and travel authorization while the immigrant petition
    is pending. Investors abroad typically use consular processing instead: the petition is filed and, after approval and
    visa availability, the immigrant visa interview happens at a U.S. consulate or embassy. Which path applies depends
    on your status, location, and visa-number rules. Confirm with an immigration attorney. Process overview:
    <a href="/eb5-investment-process">EB-5 investment process</a>. Full technical depth:
    <a href="/research/j1-f1-h1b-eb5-concurrent-filing">J-1, F-1, H-1B concurrent filing with EB-5</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What concurrent filing can unlock (decision-stage view)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Work authorization (EAD).</strong> Concurrent adjustment packages often include an application for an
      Employment Authorization Document. Timing varies and changes; do not rely on a remembered number. Check USCIS's
      official
      <a href="https://egov.uscis.gov/processing-times/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >processing times</a
      > page for current data on the relevant forms.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Travel authorization (advance parole / travel document).</strong> Concurrent packages commonly also seek
      advance parole so the applicant can travel abroad and return without abandoning the pending adjustment. This is a
      distinct benefit from the EAD. Search and plan for both by name when comparing options.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Whether a spouse can also work.</strong> Yes. A derivative spouse included on the petition can also apply
      for EAD and travel authorization through the concurrent filing process, subject to the same eligibility and
      adjudication rules as the principal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>L-1 holders.</strong> Concurrent filing applies to L-1 intracompany transferees the same way it does to
      H-1B and F-1 holders who are otherwise eligible. The petition is not limited to those two statuses. See
      <a href="/pathways/eb5-for-l1">EB-5 for L-1 visa holders</a> for L-1-specific framing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This page is the short decision-stage summary. For status-by-status technical detail, use the
    <a href="/research/j1-f1-h1b-eb5-concurrent-filing">concurrent filing research article</a>. Always verify current
    processing times at
    <a href="https://egov.uscis.gov/processing-times/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >egov.uscis.gov/processing-times</a
    >.
  </p>
</PathwayLandingLayout>
